00:04:29.603 --> 00:04:37.211
<v Host>This tournament is a classic sight of the Japanese summer. Many people watch the games on TV and cheer for the teams.

00:04:37.812 --> 00:04:40.043
<v Vocab>応援

00:04:40.444 --> 00:04:43.564
<v Host>It means cheering, or supporting a team.

00:04:44.163 --> 00:04:53.836
<v Slow>負けたチームの選手が、思い出に、球場の土を持って帰ることも有名です。

00:04:54.636 --> 00:05:00.971
<v Host>It is also famous that players on the losing team take home some dirt from the stadium field as a memory.

00:05:01.572 --> 00:05:03.803
<v Vocab>思い出

00:05:04.204 --> 00:05:08.115
<v Host>It means a memory — something you keep and remember fondly.

00:05:08.716 --> 00:05:11.716
<v Host>Let's listen to the whole story one more time.

